1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,817
That email wants your password, and it is
in a hurry.

2
00:00:05,367 --> 00:00:09,241
Five seconds is all it takes, if you check
three things.

3
00:00:10,211 --> 00:00:12,838
Sender, link, and ask.

4
00:00:14,388 --> 00:00:15,908
Check the sender domain.

5
00:00:16,878 --> 00:00:21,515
Hover before you click, and read the real
address, not the label.

6
00:00:22,485 --> 00:00:25,184
Nobody legitimate asks for a password.

7
00:00:26,734 --> 00:00:31,329
A real invoice names you. A fake one says
dear customer.

8
00:00:32,299 --> 00:00:33,899
Names are cheap to fake.

9
00:00:35,449 --> 00:00:40,068
Forty percent of the trick is a deadline.
Thirty is a threat.

10
00:00:41,038 --> 00:00:42,364
Thirty is a link.

11
00:00:43,914 --> 00:00:48,098
Report it, or delete it. Never reply to
it.

12
00:00:49,068 --> 00:00:51,686
A reply tells them the address is live.

13
00:00:53,236 --> 00:00:56,674
Hover before you click. Every single time.
